      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Yes; inserting a deload week will allow your client's central nervous system to recover from accumulated fatigue, which often causes the premature RPE of 10. Switching their volume following a pyramid scheme—starting light and progressing the load while keeping total reps steady—can also help improve quality without adding excessive taxing. These adjustments remove the stress preventing preparation for the final set, naturally reducing RPE to enable them to safely add weight and break the plateau.",
